THEOREM (rigorous): q* <= 13 ln M  (theta(q*) <= 13 ln M since every prime p<q* divides
a runner => prod_{p<q*} p | lcm(runners) <= M^13). VERIFIED: q*<=bound in every row,
and theta(q*)/ln M <= 13 always. So the FIRST FREE MODULUS is O(log M), rigorously.
